      {
        "message_id": "1538701993529573417",
        "author_username": "girsanov_27",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-17T08:12:22.958000+08:00",
        "vote_type": "P1",
        "content": "P1 - NO\n\nThis is an announcement market: the rules require an official statement clearly and unambiguously communicating a definitive termination of participation, and by name they exclude conditional withdrawals, open-ended suspensions, and mere descriptions of status. Every YES quote is one of those three:\n\n- \u201cIn the event of a breach by the other party, we too will refrain\u201d \u2192 conditional.\n- \u201cWe have stopped/suspended our commitments\u201d (Farsi: \u0645\u062a\u0648\u0642\u0641/\u062a\u0639\u0644\u06cc\u0642, never terminate/withdraw) \u2192 suspension.\n- \u201cNo negotiations currently taking place\u201d / \u201dno decision yet to restart negotiations\u201d (Araghchi, this week) \u2192 status. A pending decision to resume is the logical negation of a definitive termination.\n\nMeanwhile, within the window, Iran invoked MOU Article 5, filed a UNSC complaint over MOU breaches, and is in mediated extension talks. Prior brackets resolved NO undisputed on these same statements. Nothing new was announced, only the deadline arrived.",
        "urls": [],
        "bayesian_score": 0.7297297297297297,
        "power_weight": 0.5325054784514244
      }
