        "author_username": "jaroborzita",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-13T09:30:45.583000+08:00",
        "vote_type": "P2",
        "content": "P2 Yes\n\nVenezuela and Israel released **a historic joint statement resuming formal ties**. It is clear from the text of the statement that each government recognizes the other. In particular, Venezuela is willing to enter into official agreements and communiques with **\"the State of Israel\" as its formal counterparty**.\n\n* [Israel, Venezuela restore formal ties after 17 year break](https://www.ynetnews.com/article/hynb006oimx)\n* [Israel, Venezuela renew official ties after 17-year diplomatic freeze](https://themedialine.org/headlines/israel-venezuela-renew-official-ties-after-17-year-diplomatic-freeze/)\n* [Israel and Venezuela restore diplomatic relations](https://www.middleeasteye.net/news/israel-and-venezuela-restore-diplomatic-relations)\n\nThis is unlike the case of Lebanon, where there were genuine questions about whether the Israel-Lebanon framework agreement required cabinet approval, and where there was a lack of media uptake.\n\nThe rules do not require a specific linguistic formula whereby recognition is conveyed. For 9 examples of markets that resolved Y on similar evidence see :\n\nhttps://polymarket.com/event/will-trump-recognize-syrian-government-before-august\nhttps://polymarket.com/event/who-will-recognize-syrian-government-by-march-31\nhttps://kalshi.com/markets/kxgovtrecogsyria/syrian-government-recognition\n\nNote also that **recognition is not the same as diplomatic normalization**, and there are several other markets for normalization rather than recognition.\n\nAs to the concern raised by Thonker that Venezuela may have already recognized Israel (and merely terminated diplomatic relations in the past): if the market is not to be DOA, then it should be Y when Venezuela affirms its recognition of Israel, which it has not until now. It does not make sense to arbitrarily raise the bar for the market to an explicit declaration not required in the rules. **As a matter of fact, Venezuela does recognize the State of Israel, and today's joint statement proves it.**",
